Sent to the Legal Counsel of Ovrsea who contacted us directly after Helen’s email: 

“Dear Patricia,

Thank you for coming back to us. I understand your concern and taking your points into consideration, please find below some wordings we can propose which we believe reasonable for both parties. Our other points in the GTCs are still valid.

{quote}* Regarding clause 4.3: we included the notion of best estimates and the notion of best efforts.{quote}

{quote}* Regarding clause 7.1: we included the notion of objective evidence.{quote}

{quote}* Regarding clause 9.3: Ovrsea has a personal liability with a capped amount (clause 9.2), which we accepted. We ask you to delete clause 9.3 so that in the case of a substitute's failure, this failure is encompassed in your liability. There is no reason why Bolt should suffer a diminished liability in case the failure comes from your subcontractors. What relationship you have with them shall not impact ours, and not shall not come into consideration. {quote}

"*4.3 Quotation* 

{quote}Quotations specify the conditions for the performance of the Services by Ovrsea and their validity period. Once this validity period has expired, Ovrsea does not guarantee the maintenance of the offer conditions. {quote}

{quote}

_The departure and arrival dates communicated are given as best estimates and Ovrsea will use their best efforts to maintain their effectiveness."_{quote}

"*7.1 Prices*

{quote}Prices are exclusive of taxes on the Quotation. They are determined, taking into account: ● Information provided by the Customer on the day of the Quotation, including the number and nature of the Services to be performed, the nature, weight, characteristics, and volume of the Goods to be transported, and the routes to be taken, considering the situation on the day of the Quotation's establishment. ● Currency exchange rates on the day of issuing the Quotations. ● Conditions and rates of Ovrsea's substitutes, as well as laws, regulations, and international conventions in force on the day of issuing the Quotations. ● Fuel prices, the variation of which must be taken into account in accordance with the provisions of articles L.3222-1 and L.3222-2 of the Transport Code. 

Prices have a validity period stated on the Quotation. 

If one or more of the elements mentioned in a, b, c, and d above were modified after the acceptance of the Quotation by the Customer, including due to Ovrsea's substitutes (change in rates, in particular), opposable to the latter, the Prices will be adjusted upwards or downwards by Ovrsea to take these modifications into account. _Ovrsea will have to justify the Prices adjustments by providing objective evidence, for the changes to be opposable to the Customer._

Prices are also subject to Extraordinary Events and variable costs called surcharges (CAF / BAF / IMCO / CONGESTION (Demurrage and Detention) / AMS / ISPS / FP / ERS / WAR RISK / FUEL / SECURITY, etc.), and will be adjusted upwards or downwards by Ovrsea accordingly, without prior authorization from the Customer _provided that Ovrsea can show objective evidence supporting the variation_. 

The Customer will bear the full cost of these variable expenses and/or upward adjustment of the Price, _provided Ovrsea provides objective evidence supporting the variable expenses and/or upward adjustment of the Price._ 

Ovrsea and the Customer will be respectively responsible for their own taxes, duties, and levies of any kind, existing or to be created, that may apply directly or indirectly to the Contract."{quote}

