The issue has existed in the app since at least version CI.118.0 (November 2023) and is not related to the changes made for the opt-in improvements feature.

When a user tries to apply a campaign for the first time and taps "Claim", then selects an appropriate payment method, the {{CampaignCodesProviderImpl.paymentsDidUpdate(_ payments: [PaymentsProductFlow: PaymentsData])}} method is triggered. This method then tries to update the campaigns in {{CampaignCodesProviderImpl.updateAppliedCode(campaigns: Campaign)}} ([ref|https://github.com/bolteu/ios-app/blob/d4e723b8da8272cc902246af1ecc32a5abfa1d56/Targets/RiderCampaigns/Sources/Campaigns/CampaignCodesProvider.swift#L132]):

{noformat}let applied = codeIsAvailable(defaultCode.code, product: product) && defaultCode.autoApplicable
if applied {
  store.setAppliedCode(defaultCode.code.code, by: product)
}{noformat}

Because this is not an auto-applied campaign, {{defaultCode.autoApplicable}} is always {{false}}, which makes {{applied}} {{false}} as well, resulting in the campaign not being applied.

