Lisa has come back with clarifications: 



* *re/ Zimbabwe (Tracker / DPO Appointment)*: The reference to Sam as DPO is referring to Sam's appointment as Global DPO for Bolt OU.
* *Self Assessment Form Completion*: the regulations refer to the self assessment form being made available on POTRAZ's website (see Reg 3.(1). I've double checked the website and it doesn't seem that the self assessment form has been set up yet on the website. The self assessment form (DP1) is, however, included as the First Schedule in the Regulations. The regulations are still in draft form, to my recollection, which is likely the reason for the forms not yet being published on POTRAZ's website.
* *Reference only to the Cyber and Data Protection Regulations, 2022 (and not to Zimbabwe's DPA) in the memorandum*: The memorandum deals specifically with the requirements for the licensing and registration of data controllers, which is a new requirement being introduced by way of the regulations. The DPA does not cover licensing and registration of data controllers. The DPA does, however, address the controller's obligation to notify the relevant authority prior to processing personal data as well as to notify the authority of the appointment of a DPO. I'm happy to prepare a complementary memorandum to delve into these topics further.



Confirmed with Sam and asked to prepare a Complimentary memo on Friday 05/07: 



