Hey, [~accountid:62d7b457807cf6f78ca9d117]! I reviewed the information provided in the ticket. As far as I understand we will be selling bio products produced, packed and labelled by someone else. This would fall under resale activity. From the information provided by Sorina there is a distinction in terms of requirements that apply to sale and distribution activity. It is not clear how sale and distribution are defined and in which category we would fall. 

Short summary: 

* If we distribute goods - we need to register the activity with the authority;
* If we sell goods - we can be exempt from registration, but we need to declare our activity.

I think that we fall under “sale” activity because we do not act as a distributor per se. Also, in appendix 9 that is a declaration to be submitted to the authority in case we fall under “sale” activity it is required to be confirmed by the seller that:

* it sells prepackaged ecological products directly to the consumer or end user;
* it does not produce, prepare and store the distributed products other than in connection with the point of sale;
* it does not import such products from a third country;
* it does not subcontract such activities to another operator.

We need to confirm with the business the above. Also, we will be required to disclose all locations of sale, but technically, consumers are not allowed to enter these, so it is a bit complicated.

I suggest contacting Andrei Georgescu and ask to help us - confirm which requirements will apply to us and help to register activity if this is required. I would also mentioned specifically that Bolt Market operates using “dark store” model. If no registration will be required, i.e. we fall under “sale” activity, we need to clarify how to go about sale points. I think we are capable of preparing the declaration ourselves in case we fall under “sale” activity as the form is provided in appendix 9 of the act.

